From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:04:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] windows.web: implement HttpRequestMessage and
 HttpResponseMessage.

The class Office's React Native host reaches for once it has an HttpClient,
and the one it gets back.  Both are records -- a caller fills one in, hands it
to a client and reads the other back -- so both are implemented outright, apart
from the two properties whose type belongs to a part of the namespace that is
not here yet, which say so.

Their header collections are the reason for stringmap.c.  Each collection is
an IMap<HSTRING, HSTRING> with typed accessors layered on top, and the host
reaches them as the map: both that interface and its iterable are in
react-native-win32.dll.  wintypes has a map for IInspectable values, which is
the wrong value type and not exported besides, so this is the string one, in
one place rather than written out once per collection.  Header names compare
without regard to case, as the protocol says, while the name the caller
inserted is the name given back.

IsSuccessStatusCode answers for the whole 2xx range rather than the codes the
enum happens to name, so a 299 from a server that invented one is still a
success, and EnsureSuccessStatusCode fails on anything else instead of
returning a response the caller would read as good.

tools/winrtprobe covers both: a header round-trips, a differently-cased name
finds it, re-inserting replaces rather than duplicates, removing an absent one
is E_BOUNDS, and the success rule is checked at 200, 299 and 404.  44 of 44
checks pass against the prefix Office runs in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 35d0a67dd82177b7ef24e232ae1ba34f08fd64b0)

